+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`; it
+returns the referenced value and throws when the pointer is syntactically invalid or does not resolve
+to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- `""` refers to the whole document; otherwise the pointer must start with `/`.
+- `~0` -> `~`, `~1` -> `/` (decoded `~1` first, then `~0`); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- Objects: reference token is an own property key. Arrays: token must be `0` or digits without leading
+  zeros and within bounds; `-` (past the end) does not resolve to a value; non-numeric tokens fail.
+- Primitives cannot be traversed. Inherited properties (e.g. `__proto__`) never resolve.
